{title: 585 - When Christ Was Lifted From the Earth}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #585 • ST. BOTOLPH • 14.17}
{lyricist: Brian Wren}
{composer: Gordon Slater}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 585}
{meta: tune ST. BOTOLPH}
{meta: meter 14.17}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]When Christ [Bm]was [A]lifted [Em/G]from [G]the [Bm]earth [A/C#]His [D]arms stretched [G]out above
[F#m]Through [G]every [A]culture, [F#m]every birth, to [A7]draw [Bm]an [D/A]answering [A7]love.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Still east [Bm]and [A]west [Bm]His [Em/G]love [G]extends [A/C#]and [D]always, [G]near or [Em]far,
[F#m]He [G]calls [A7/E]and [Bm]claims [A]us [F#m]as [G]His [Em]friends [F#m]and loves [D/A]us [Em/G]as [G]we [A7]are.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Where generation, [Em/G]class, [G]or [A]race [Bm]divides [D/F#]us [G]to our [Em]shame,
[F#m]He [G]sees [A7/E]not [Bm]labels [F#m]but [G]a [F#m]face, a [A7]person [Em/G]and [G]a [A7]name.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]Thus freely [A]loved, [Bm]tho' [Em/G]fully [Bm]known, [A/C#]may [D]I in [G]Christ be [Em]free
[F#m]To [G]welcome [Bm]and [G]accept His [F#m]own as [A7]Christ [Bm]accepted [A7]me.
{end_of_verse}
